WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:08.300
Liquid LSD plays up to three video sources at once, each on its own deck: A, B and BG.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.600
Every deck runs its video through a chain of three effects.

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:20.100
A transition mixes Deck A and Deck B. The crossfader moves between them.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:25.600
Deck BG fills in behind them, wherever their mix is transparent.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:31.900
The mix then runs through three master effects, and out to your audience.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:41.100
Three decks reach the audience. A fourth, Deck PV, is your private preview, with its own effects.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:49.100
Every deck works the same way. Most of the time a deck plays a generator, a shader that draws video live.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:55.900
Dozens come with the app, and you can add your own: they use ISF, an open shader format.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:01:03.100
A deck can also show live video from another app, over Spout, Syphon or PipeWire.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:10.400
Each generator has its own parameters. Wave Ripples has Sources, Wavelength and Wave Speed.

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.100
Metaballs has Balls, Ball Size and Merge.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.500
Tunnel Scenes has Scene, Sides and Twist.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:28.100
Any parameter can be turned with an on-screen knob, or driven by audio, an LFO, a sequencer or a hardware controller.

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:34.600
Effects work the same way. Kaleidoscope has Segments, Rotation and Zoom.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:39.800
The next slot has its own effect, with its own parameters.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:48.400
Order matters: Pixelate before Kaleidoscope looks different from Pixelate after it.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:54.400
Transitions have parameters too. Vortex Swirl has Rotations and Radius.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:59.400
Film Burn has its own, controlled the same way.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:03.000
And the master chain works just like a deck's.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.000
Now let's see where all of this lives in the app.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.500
The big screen on the right is the master output: what your audience sees.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:20.000
Below it, a preview of each of the four decks: A, B, BG and PV.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:26.000
A and B are the main decks. The crossfader mixes between them.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.500
BG is the background deck: it is drawn behind A and B.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:36.900
Its level starts at zero. Drag its fader up and BG appears behind deck A.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.900
Deck A draws only part of the frame, so BG fills in around it.

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:48.900
PV is the preview deck. Try things out here: the audience never sees it.

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:55.900
On the left is the Perform view: rows of knobs, grouped into pages. This is the A/B page.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:02.000
The BG/PV page holds the BG and PV decks.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:10.100
MIXER holds the deck levels, the master FX chain, transitions and the clock.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:19.000
Back to A/B. Perform is one of three views; the other two are Edit (Ch. 6 at 6:46) and Library (Ch. 7 at 7:35).

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:26.000
Every deck has two rows. The top row, SRC, is its source: the shader that draws the picture.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.000
The row below is the deck's FX chain. Here it is switched off.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:38.500
BYPASS turns the whole chain on or off. Click it, and the picture runs through the effects.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:42.000
More on FX in Ch. 5 at 5:12. Sources first.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Click the source name to browse sources and presets for that deck.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:55.600
Click a source in the list and it loads straight into the deck.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:04:01.400
Each click swaps the deck's source. Watch deck A's preview and the output.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:03.900
And back to Kifs.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:09.900
Save stores the deck's source and all its settings as a preset.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:15.900
The gear opens the Edit view with every parameter of the row (Ch. 6 at 6:46).

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:21.900
The FX row below is the deck's effect chain (Ch. 5 at 5:12).

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:27.900
Every row has four knobs, mapped to that row's most useful parameters.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:32.100
Drag up or right to turn a knob up...

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.100
...and down or left to turn it down.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:43.100
Hold Shift while dragging for fine control. Double-click a knob to type a value.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:55.100
Under the output is the crossfader. It blends deck A into deck B.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:05:01.100
The same crossfader is the first knob of the Transitions row on the MIXER page.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:06.100
Turn it and the crossfader under the output follows.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:13.000
The other knobs shape the transition: how deck A becomes deck B.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:19.000
Every deck has an FX chain with three slots. The master has one too.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:25.000
The picture flows through the slots from left to right: slot 1, then 2, then 3.

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:33.500
So order matters. Here Kaleidoscope folds the image, then Polar Tunnel wraps the result into a tunnel.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:40.500
Swap them, and the tunnel is folded instead. Same effects, a very different picture.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:47.000
Drag a slot onto another to reorder the chain.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:54.700
The power button switches one slot off without removing it.

00:05:54.700 --> 00:06:01.200
Each slot's knob is that effect's Metaknob: one knob that drives its main parameters.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:07.300
The Super Knob turns the Metaknobs of every linked slot at once.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:13.300
A slot joins in when the Super Knob passes its current value, so nothing jumps.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:21.300
The link button above a slot adds it to the Super Knob or takes it out. Click to unlink Polar Tunnel.

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:27.800
Now the Super Knob moves only the linked slots. Polar Tunnel stays put.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:31.600
Click again to link it back.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:38.000
The link beside the Super Knob links or unlinks all slots at once.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:46.500
The master FX chain on the MIXER page works the same way. It runs after the crossfader, on the final mix.

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:51.400
The gear on a row opens the Edit view.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:57.400
Edit lists every parameter of the deck's source, not only the four on the knobs.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:03.400
K1 to K4 mark the parameters that sit on the row's four knobs.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:09.400
VAL sets a parameter's value. LFO and the other columns add modulation.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:16.400
Click a parameter to see and edit its properties.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:23.400
The FX tab shows the deck's chain: wet/dry, the Super Knob and every slot's parameters.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:29.400
These checkboxes are another way to choose which slots follow the Super Knob.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:35.900
The tabs on the far left jump to the other decks and to the mixer.

00:07:35.900 --> 00:07:42.300
The Library view fills the screen with your sources, effects and presets.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:48.300
Tabs switch between sources, FX, transitions, queues and macros.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:56.800
Search finds items by name, tag or folder.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.800
Preferences, under General, has the theme.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:08.300
There are two: dark, and this light one for bright rooms.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:14.300
